// Fused select scrutinee-refire swallowed (aug05h ryouko reactive
// divergence_000000, hand-reduced): the node-walk re-emits a selected
// arm's ridden value on EVERY scrutinee delivery (probed: const arms,
// both pattern kinds, one emission per injection epoch, both modes).
// The fused select's merge taint cache rebuilt its substitution disc
// as clean|STALE ("didn't fire" — right for rides triggered by other
// inputs), so a scrutinee-driven re-fire whose fresh computation
// tainted (here: the fold callback's capture is a catch-fed binding
// that never fires, so each slot taints) rode the cached value STALE
// and the output freshness gate swallowed it — interp emitted the
// ridden 2 on the injection epoch, jit emitted nothing. Fix: AND the
// scrutinee's STALE into the merged disc after the cache (idempotent
// on the normal path; skipped for TAINTED results to keep TAINT⟹STALE
// and the no-history bottom). Load-bearing conjunction, all reduced:
// reactive connect-array source + callee-body select taking the error
// arm through ?/catch reading an input + BINDING-pattern outer select
// (the wildcard variant de-fuses) + fold with the catch capture.
// schedule-v1: cap=80 events=640; in0=i64:1
{let v0: Array<i64> = []; v0 <- in0 ~ array::push(v0, in0); let v8 = |v9: i64| select v9 {i64:0 => (i64:1 + v9), _ => error(true)}; let v10 = (try (v8(i64:1))? catch(e) => (-(in0))); let v11: i64 = select in0 {v11 => array::fold(v0, i64:2, |v12, x| v10)}; v11}
